# Check global rules first

When working in this project, ALWAYS follow Andre's machine-level global rules in
`C:\Users\User\.cursor\rules\` — especially:

- `python-version-policy.mdc` — which Python to use (default = newest installed, 3.14.x).
- `andre-pc-specs.mdc` and `andre-user-context.mdc` — PC + user background.

Also read the Information Hierarchy when present: `_ABOUT-ME/*.md`, the root `AGENTS.md`,
and this project's `PROJECT.md`.

**Python:** create venvs with the newest Python (`py -3.14 -m venv .venv`) unless a safety
issue or a pinned exception in `python-version-policy.mdc` applies.
